he right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{S}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "948eac23-81d2-5cc0-800b-0edc863e2953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388211} {:answer/id #uuid "952de722-8203-5743-8593-c71db966ae3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388212} {:answer/id #uuid "cce08128-0360-55fa-b3b2-a44378c80726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388213} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a26f5d-0602-5ec5-83d9-2aa6bd1bdcf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388214} {:answer/id #uuid "d1eda9a4-a5ea-5838-86e1-566847652b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388213} :answer-field/id #uuid "788280f7-1f4b-5462-8a7a-cd446a5868f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388210}] :question/id #uuid "23d98e62-6043-5354-9621-545d60a12bf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-131379" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4683baa-7e31-565a-90dd-81bc97617456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402004} {:answer/id #uuid "e66e39bf-af21-54ee-9c01-1e665e79afcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402005} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb3bda1-f364-5e06-b3f9-1ec1294cdafe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402006} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae71a29-b56a-5e44-b3f7-481f0faef4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402007} {:answer/id #uuid "e81114b5-b5d4-5ed1-9aad-cfda69edeb8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402004} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce793d72-97c8-5680-9b23-e9cde7d661bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402003}] :question/id #uuid "1fb0889d-6fed-5243-aaf7-929089854f2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31954" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $D$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${D}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $D$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $D$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${D}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351e7f30-9491-58fc-8cf5-793274bcf323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417364} {:answer/id #uuid "36ed8b6e-c128-5d01-928b-08f774f8d809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417365} {:answer/id #uuid "7e84734a-f76d-51fa-a6d7-e244eb448774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417370} {:answer/id #uuid "8dbc9696-4140-550a-b72f-debd09d5fe0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417371} {:answer/id #uuid "f8aa4dff-702b-54c5-9a1b-1549247cc0ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417365} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e6a2e19-fc40-5f23-8312-fc7a5a3459ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417375}] :question/id #uuid "bcd8ebdd-840f-56b3-b01b-b55941f100d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131383" :question/problem "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $D$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${D}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $D$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $D$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${D}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{D}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix Calculated Using Row Operations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115251 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115080 :question/id #uuid "ff4b4389-d8ff-5b48-904b-ff405abb4e48" :question/math-academy-id "e-4725" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2 \\,$ and $\\, R_2 :=  R_2+(-1)R_1?$\n\n![](images/e0/e034f65af225ce46015a5accae774a24eed8617590a583a2a885b4b1c5332103.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77d78574-a17c-5fc3-8c14-3aaec7753b3c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115851 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85a4846e-0db5-5f87-8026-156fae3fa831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114044} {:answer/id #uuid "a75dd5fa-a7ff-5795-a231-591fc4e5d8f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114045} {:answer/id #uuid "d81a9c35-0038-5288-aa55-524b9b84d051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114046} {:answer/id #uuid "ea58dd7e-0d86-5f45-9b1d-d6c828308290" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114047} {:answer/id #uuid "4758b958-2022-54c2-9d36-13d6add8a54d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114048}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7081b7ea-6bf5-5221-8156-3d02e1b8b6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114043}] :question/id #uuid "04cb1085-6ee9-50b3-9586-c94a321a602e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42999" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2 \\cdot 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_{1}:=R_{1} + (-1)R_{2}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-2)R_{1}$?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d1574dd-091a-52ae-8eb0-535fd3914634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} {:answer/id #uuid "7586863f-229d-578d-ac84-f0e761139eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460005} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec46523-5df6-5a30-a264-03c885caa2bd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed431171-2bbf-5c8c-afad-a46ecfc1b548" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460007} {:answer/id #uuid "8cfdbbbb-5343-5c70-85ff-8ea0242e36fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460008} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90e3cb2-cf8d-5f7e-8a1d-7e3fced79e84" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "849f41f5-f501-53ee-8ecc-b0fca7647ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} {:answer/id #uuid "b44c80de-5afb-5ae0-9c0e-9042718b52cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460009} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b060f26-347b-584a-9045-d8d27b9e7501" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460871}] :question/id #uuid "90c835e0-83aa-519b-9995-715569dd5d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-43000" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85584b3a-c6d4-52ce-a49a-aa5715567882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463904} {:answer/id #uuid "cf095273-2cd2-5877-9b70-2ae96d4c801f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17