the following is a vector $x$ at which the minimum is attained?" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -17 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-20:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-20)I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -17 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}+20\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}19 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 27\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-20)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "659e6953-7cee-5b96-970f-fa397b86ee27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388526} {:answer/id #uuid "326d7edd-18b0-5a3b-b08d-0b77a365bbd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388527} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f8657c-b325