c{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2daa7e54-1e63-51fd-a83f-c84ab1ec9d14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442108} {:answer/id #uuid "44864e9b-3b6d-5ead-83f1-bf2b06aa99bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442109} {:answer/id #uuid "47e556d0-ace5-5cd4-bce8-0b8edffbc42a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442110} {:answer/id #uuid "b628a5cd-923e-5683-b6ff-5e0fdf447fc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442111} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d0fa24-c8cf-52e6-90a5-639dbcfbac97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442108} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a8a33df-b62e-5f61-90ea-9cf4c2ac4093" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442113}] :question/id #uuid "95026062-b044-5134-829b-f9813c55ce41" :question/math-academy-id "q-170503" :question/problem "The minimum value of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3},$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to $-10.$ Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the minimum is attained?" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-10:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-10)I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}+10\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-10)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d3a7fdb-eefe-51a3-9ec9-f7c801ef2416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513564} {:answer/id #uuid "7200c83a-2142-5d00-85db-a56671970e08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513836} {:answer/id #uuid "7223184f-b1ee-5d86-a4ef-23d7fc3ee742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/