he corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-4)I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-(-4)\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-4)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$  \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d9e2ab8-f0d5-5abe-b74e-db6a46609bb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492276} {:answer/id #uuid "208b060c-d7f6-5417-9e03-796577024e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492282} {:answer/id #uuid "96521b38-e0b7-58e6-b1db-eeedf6a34c29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492507} {:answer/id #uuid "c0497484-5b80-5f14-9367-302334efa418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492600} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b05c42-2662-52e1-be4f-95016554eeb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :