 {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555591} :answer-field/id #uuid "593656c5-9d16-5dfd-b341-863c47c4d9b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555680}] :question/id #uuid "44c4828d-5d0a-5c06-aad5-ea02f733cf44" :question/math-academy-id "q-110476" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation \n${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43dc20c6-76f4-5f40-a083-a68fff62c7a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555144} {:answer/id #uuid "89b8174c-7ba1-5290-9544-eefeb40cdcfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555320} {:answer/id #uuid "9114918e-0981-5c69-81c4-192ab15eea5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555341} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c1d932-65e6-50ad-8efd-0e962ff77a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555561} {:answer/id #uuid "e700ce2b-8be4-5604-877b-03482d66f546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555567} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ccaad93-79fb-5e66-a9e7-978681d178cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555691}] :question/id #uuid "5e29c468-7ba6-5997-83d8-49458f8bde8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-110470" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Left Multiplication Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133744 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133554 :question/id #uuid "6e47a532-ba7a-5692-961b-eabc743d74e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4734" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad\n\tR_1:=6R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/d2/d2425878812bb00748c5250dd877655a7d01faab33e148593be2a6c2de98ac4e.svg)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/c7/c741f5faf39a8bc1606d64e906162bbd5b67b3dfd88af2372f43e96736de6bb5.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00b69189-1ae1-5625-adfb-e5460845c776" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134188 :question/answer-fields 